          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "نکلوانا — nikalvānā — \"to withdraw (money); to have (something) taken out\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سارا نے بینک سے پیسے نکلوائے۔ sārā ne baink se paise nikalvāe. Sara took some money out of the bank."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with نے (he or she …): اس نے رقم نکلوائی, us ne raqam nikalvāī."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "نکلوانا (nikalvānā) is built on نکلنا, \"to come out\", with the ending -vā- for getting someone else to do it: you have the bank take your money out. نکلنا comes from niṣkalati, a form CDIAL reconstructs (CDIAL 7478)."
            }
          ]
        },
